{"id":"chatcmpl-b774a055-c27e-4407-95c2-beadd9e88fc5","object":"chat.completion","created":1795230560,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task shows a robust strategy for resolving laterality (left vs right) in medical imaging when an initial expert tool returns a negative or ambiguous result. The key move is to cross-validate with a second, independent grounding/localization tool and then confirm the specific anatomical landmark (e.g., 'L' marker, axilla) before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any binary localization question where a single tool's negative output is unreliable.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a primary expert tool returns a negative or null result for a finding that the options imply exists, treat it as unreliable and escalate to an independent grounding/localization tool rather than concluding 'absent'.\",\n    \"For laterality (left/right) questions, always verify using an explicit anatomical side marker or landmark (e.g., 'L' label, axilla, cardiac silhouette) rather than relying on image orientation alone.\",\n    \"Use phrase-level grounding on the specific finding+location candidate to confirm the option's exact wording matches the localized evidence before selecting.\",\n    \"Cross-check findings across at least two independent tools when the answer hinges on a single binary distinction; agreement between tools justifies the final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Prefer grounded localization tools over pure classification when laterality or precise location matters; confirm with side markers.\",\n    \"Binary-choice verification\": \"When options differ only by one attribute (side, segment, lobe), isolate and verify that single attribute with a targeted query.\",\n    \"Tool disagreement handling\": \"If one tool says 'absent' but options presuppose presence, do not trust the negative—seek a second modality/tool before answering.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding exists via an independent grounding tool before answering a presence-implying option set.\",\n    \"Verify laterality using an explicit side marker or anatomical landmark (e.g., 'L' label, axilla) and match it to the chosen option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":538,"total_tokens":957,"completion_tokens":419,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":538},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":419}}}